{{Term/Store|Silent Princess|Silent Princesses|Series, BotW, TotK, AoC, AoI|plural}} are recurring [[Item]]s in {{TLoZ Series}}.{{Exp Game|BotW, TotK, AoC}}<ref name="BotW Inventory"/><ref name="TotK Inventory"/><ref name="AoC Material"/><ref name="AoI Materials"/>

==Location and Uses==
==={{BotW|-}}===
{{Compendium/Extract|Silent Princess}}
The Silent Princess is a rare, endangered [[Flower]] species.<ref name="BotW Zelda"/> A century before the events of {{BotW|-}}, the plant could not be grown domestically, thriving only out in the wild.<ref name="BotW Zelda 2"/> By the time {{BotW|-}} takes place, the Silent Princess was feared to have gone extinct but was then spotted growing in the wild.<ref name="BotW Inventory"/> The flower was said to have been a favorite of [[Princess Zelda]], which is confirmed in the [[Recovered Memory]] [[Silent Princess (Memory)|Silent Princess]].<ref name="BotW Inventory"/><ref name="BotW Adventure Log"/>

During {{BotW|-}}, [[Link]] can find Silent Princesses growing near [[Great Fairy Fountain]]s across [[Hyrule Kingdom]]. The Silent Princess can be used in a [[Meal]] or [[Elixir]] to grant [[Link]] the [[Stealth Up]] [[Added Effect]]. They can also be made into White [[Dye]] at the [[Kochi Dye Shop]].

Married couple [[Tye]] and [[Sorelia]] can be found searching for the Silent Princess.<ref name="BotW Tye"/> There is a legend if you swear your love on one, you will live a charmed life with your partner.<ref name="BotW Tye 2"/> However, they've been unsuccessful in their quest.<ref name="BotW Tye 3"/>

